{"title":"2024 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jimmy wrote four tests last week. The average of his marks on the first, second and third tests was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/339baf6df71777af266e6259546917b0742caf2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. The average of his marks on the second, third and fourth tests was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. His mark on the fourth test was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times his mark on the first test. Determine his mark on the fourth test.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the marks Jimmy got on the first, second, and third tests, respectively. Since his mark on the fourth test was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times his mark on the first test, he got <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6ea4756efa52a156029529aba37a305a5cb496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> marks on the fourth test.\n</p><p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic_mean\" title=\"Arithmetic mean\">arithmetic means</a>, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef1a8380fe190129ae9e426cc8cf20ea8107a24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a + b + c}{3} = 65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/6/716065e30b12594a5348fcb9ccee11d9406defb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b + c + 2a}{3} = 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"127\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Multiplying both equations by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get rid of the fractions, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/4/894bf33c8ed493140636a32df9931aca489a55d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = 65 \\times 3 = 195$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"197\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36fe11e61e97e776c8964581d6706ccc90ab8c7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a + b + c = 80 \\times 3 = 240$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"206\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e06d02ec950fabbe8bbf1319d747c1069a1a39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = 195$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa9d4e826535ff3441c6a006148c62fbd5fa3b0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a + b + c = 240$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"16\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f8321681c0467ce1a5d0cde6b66879eb67147d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a + b + c - a - b - c = 240 - 195$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"274\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5073431893e72faf624b0ff92249636a19500f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Since he got <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> marks on the first test and he had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times that on his fourth test, he must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09eb30c3533872288cf352475b774efee93c9c7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 \\times 2 = \\boxed{90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" /> marks on the fourth test.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017233428\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.032 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 76/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3600/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.746      1 2024_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    7.746      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35993:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017233428 and revision id 279592. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}